# Source and build config — only dist/ is needed at runtime.
#
# These are anchored with a leading slash because the patterns are gitignore
# semantics: a bare "src/" matches at EVERY depth, so it also deletes
# node_modules/<pkg>/src. That shipped a debug/ with nothing in it but a
# package.json pointing main at the ./src/index.js that had just been stripped,
# and debug is reachable from express inside the MCP SDK. Nothing broke only
# because this server speaks stdio and never loads the HTTP transports. The
# patterns below that are not anchored cost bundle size at worst, never a
# missing module.
/src/
/test/
/tsconfig.json
/package-lock.json

# Docs (the manifest carries its own description)
docs/
DESKTOP_EXTENSION.md

# Local / VCS clutter
.git/
.github/
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/

# Never ship a previously built bundle inside a new one
*.mcpb
*.dxt
